+-- migration: 8
+-- name: engine_reads_witness_panel
+-- rollback: NONE as a migration, but the grants below can be reversed by hand with
+--   REVOKE ALL ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA witness FROM cd_engine and
+--   REVOKE ALL ON SCHEMA witness FROM cd_engine, which destroys no data. Migrations here
+--   remain forward-only (PBG-DATA-002).
+--
+-- The serving layer shows the panel next to the two dials, and the process that assembles
+-- that view runs as cd_engine. Today it cannot read the panel row at all, so the surface
+-- has to be assembled in two passes by two different identities. This gives cd_engine the
+-- read it needs and nothing else: SELECT only, no INSERT, no UPDATE, no DELETE. The
+-- append-only posture of migration 7 is untouched.
+
+GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA witness TO cd_engine;
+
+GRANT SELECT ON witness.observation TO cd_engine;
+GRANT SELECT ON witness.reading TO cd_engine;
